WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.940
(light music)

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:02.880
- [Narrator] Huawei, the
world's largest maker

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.180
of telecom equipment
became a global leader

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.840
in designing cutting edge chips,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.730
rivaling those made by
Samsung, Apple and Nvidia,

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.530
but ever since the US imposed
sanctions against Huawei

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.230
in 2019, the Chinese tech
giant has been losing

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.940
it's foothold in the
global smartphone market.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.010
- The restrictions that
came down on Huawei

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:24.520
in 2019 certainly took
the company by surprise.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.147
The US for a long time saw the company as

00:00:27.147 --> 00:00:29.230
a national security threat,

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.180
but it took quite a few
years for Washington

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.380
to kind of really mobilize itself and take

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.530
some serious action against the company.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.350
- [Narrator] A spike in
demand has contributed

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.830
to the global chip shortage,

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:42.170
but ongoing US China political frictions

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.910
have exacerbated the situation for Huawei.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.410
So what led the us to impose restrictions

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.380
on the Chinese tech giant?

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.870
First, the US has long seen Huawei as

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.640
a national security threat,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.230
especially as it was advancing
so quickly in 5G technology.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.850
- This was seen as a problem
amongst some US policymakers

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:03.550
who have long been concerned that Huawei

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:06.990
telecommunications gear can
in some way be intercepted

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.280
or tapped by the Chinese government.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.910
- [Narrator] Huawei has
denied this allegation.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.670
Two more reasons for the
restrictions, allegations

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.950
of intellectual property
theft and violation

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.350
of trade sanctions.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:21.260
In 2019, the US charged
Huawei with attempting

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.470
to steal trade secrets from T-Mobile

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.760
and with violating trade
sanctions against Iran.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.960
- The alleged fraudulent
financial schemes used

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.730
by Huawei and its chief financial officer

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:34.910
were not just illegal, but
detrimental to the security

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.750
of the United States.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.310
- [Narrator] Huawei previously denied

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.680
all of these allegations,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.290
but in September the
company CFO reached a deal

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.860
with the US admitting
to some wrongdoing in

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.890
the Iran trade sanctions case.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.500
Both cases are still ongoing.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.230
Later in 2019 the US placed Huawei on

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.640
what's called the Entity List,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.020
banning US companies
like Google and Qualcomm

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.700
from working with Huawei.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.450
Then in 2020, the US tightened the terms

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.900
of the Entity Listing twice,

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.670
cutting Huawei off from
its own chip manufacturers

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:07.081
and then later blocking
Huawei from accessing any chip

00:02:07.081 --> 00:02:09.261
built using US technology.

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:12.910
- Us technology is so deeply
embedded in the supply chain.

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:17.020
So, this was a truly destructive
measure that blocked the

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:22.010
company from chip makers, not
just in US, but in Taiwan,

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:24.350
in Europe, even in mainland China.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.730
- Despite the restrictions,
any company that wants

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.860
to sell to Huawei can apply for a license

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.230
from the US government.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.300
But these are often difficult to get.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.612
- For example, Qualcomm is able to sell

00:02:34.612 --> 00:02:37.030
4G chip technology to Huawei.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:39.261
Other companies are selling
more rudimentary chips

00:02:39.261 --> 00:02:41.710
to Huawei, and you can
see that that's really

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:45.290
an offshoot of this underlying
desire and policy circles

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.750
in Washington to reign
in Huawei's 5G technology

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.930
without totally sort of
choking off the company

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.820
from any components whatsoever.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:55.570
- Since September 2020,
Huawei has been relying

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.050
on its stockpile of chips,

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.110
but its supply is now running low.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.320
Huawei is investing in
domestic chip makers,

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.110
but it could still take
them years to catch up

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.530
to US technology.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.380
Huawei released a new phone in July,

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:08.580
but without high-tech
chips it can't connect

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.010
to 5G networks and analysts say it will

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.950
struggle to compete globally.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.870
In September, Huawei deputy
chairman, Eric Schuh said

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.010
the company's smartphone revenue will drop

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:21.020
by up to $40 billion this year.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.490
And so far there haven't been
any signs from Washington

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.550
that the US will loosen
these restrictions.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:29.300
- You're seeing Huawei pull back on 5G.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.150
You're seeing Huawei
lose out on 5G contracts.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.350
You're seeing it's 5G phone
sales totally collapse.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:38.112
And in many ways this was the
goal of some of the sanctions.

00:03:38.112 --> 00:03:40.695
(bouncy music)

